"rel_precision":0.6666666666666666,"rel_recall":1.0,"rel_f1":0.8,"rel_tp":2,"rel_fp":1,"rel_fn":0},"pairs":[{"head":"timolol maleate","tail":"bradycardia and hypotension","head_id":"1","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"pilocarpine nitrate","tail":"bradycardia and hypotension","head_id":"2","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"halothane","tail":"bradycardia and hypotension","head_id":"3","tail_id":"1"}],"relations":["1 | 1","2 | 1","3 | 1"],"text":"Intraoperative bradycardia and hypotension associated with timolol and pilocarpine eye drops. A 69-yr-old man, who was concurrently being treated with pilocarpine nitrate and timolol maleate eye drops, developed a bradycardia and became hypotensive during halothane anaesthesia. Both timolol and pilocarpine were subsequently identified in a 24-h collection of urine. Timolol (but not pilocarpine) was detected in a sample of plasma removed during surgery; the plasma concentration of timolol (2.6 ng ml-1) was consistent with partial beta-adrenoceptor blockade. It is postulated that this action may have been enhanced during halothane anaesthesia with resultant bradycardia and hypotension. Pilocarpine may have had a contributory effect."}